sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: DECISIONS scope (instance.rename record-only, R1); rule 1 (checkout read from Node agent reports); a new domain admits route.update (own chart); DECISIONS 2 (DNS held).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:rename
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane A icon=server pill=observer tone=amber
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant A as Node agent<br/>orbit-agent
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  loop continuously, on change
    Note over A: Observe checkouts<br/>branch, HEAD, origin
    %%> What it observes:
    %%> - each Instance checkout on Node 12: its symbolic `HEAD`, origin, owner and layout
    %%> Runs as:
    %%> - read-only; the Node agent never changes a Node
    A->>GW: Report observations<br/>with observed_at
    %%> What it sends:
    %%> - what changed since the last report, with the time it was observed
    Note over GW: Store latest facts<br/>per Node, per checkout
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Gateway knows which branch each checkout has checked out
  end
  CLI->>GW: instance:rename 42<br/>--branch=t3code/login-redirect
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:rename 42 --branch=t3code/login-redirect`
  %%> - syntax: `<instance> [--branch=BRANCH] [--domain=HOST] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Before:
  %%> - rename the branch in the checkout first: `git branch -m t3code/login-redirect`
  %%> What it does not do:
  %%> - rename the Instance, move its directory, or change Git `HEAD`
  %%> With `--domain`:
  %%> - also moves the Instance's Route to the new domain
  Note over GW: Check against the facts<br/>HEAD names the branch
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12, which runs Instance 42
  %%> - Instance 42 is an active development checkout, not a linked worktree or production
  %%> - no other lifecycle change holds Instance 42
  %%> Checks in the agent's latest report:
  %%> - symbolic `HEAD` names `t3code/login-redirect`
  %%> - the origin still is Project 7's repository
  %%> - the report is fresh enough to trust
  %%> Allowed:
  %%> - dirty or unpublished source
  alt branch is checked out
    Note over GW: Record the branch<br/>R1: no task, no run
    %%> Result:
    %%> - `selected_branch` and `branch_override` of Instance 42 become `t3code/login-redirect`
    %%> - the already recorded branch keeps its existing override
    %%> - no Swamp run starts (R1)
    %%> Later:
    %%> - removal, cloning and doctor check the new branch
    opt --domain given
      Note over GW: Admit a route.update<br/>task #5160 · own chart
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - admits a `route.update` task for the Route of Instance 42, with the new domain
      %%> - the Route change has its own chart; rename only starts it
      %%> Today:
      %%> - `--domain` returns `operation.kind_unavailable`
      GW->>SW: Start route.update run<br/>operation-route-update
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209) for the Route change
      Note over SW: DNS publication held<br/>open: Nick decides
      %%> Open:
      %%> - DNS publication for Routes is on hold (`native-dns-takeover-held`)
      %%> - until Nick decides, the Route change is same-Node work only
    end
    GW-->>CLI: Branch recorded<br/>Instance 42 · task #5160 if any
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the result at once
    %%> - with `--domain`, also the `route.update` task number to follow
  else not checked out or refused
    GW--xCLI: 422 Refused<br/>instance.branch_not_checked_out
    %%> When:
    %%> - `HEAD` names another branch or is detached
    %%> - or Instance 42 is not an active development checkout
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing is recorded
  else agent silent too long
    GW--xCLI: Can't verify<br/>Node 12 facts too old
    %%> When:
    %%> - the Node agent hasn't reported recently, so the Gateway can't trust what it knows
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing is recorded; try again when the agent reports
  end
  opt route.update admitted
    loop every 2 s until terminal
      CLI->>GW: operation:show #5160
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - follows the Route change every 2 seconds until it has ended
      GW-->>CLI: status + result
      %%> Returns:
      %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
    end
  end
